meta {
  name: Create Provider (Chat - OpenRouter)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/ai_provider_configs
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{admin_username}}
  password: {{admin_password}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/ld+json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "openrouter-chat-recruteurs",
    "usage": "chat",
    "provider": "api_endpoint",
    "apiEndpoint": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions",
    "apiKey": "{{openrouter_api_key}}",
    "model": "minimax/minimax-m2.7:free",
    "isActive": true,
    "isDefault": true
  }
}

docs {
  Cloud/free-tier alternative to "Create Provider (Chat)" (which targets local
  Ollama) -- used by the "Assistant Recruteurs" scenario so the agent works
  without a local Ollama server (prod has none either, see backend/.env.prod).

  model: OpenRouter's free-tier catalog rotates -- "openai/gpt-oss-20b:free"
  (the model originally configured in .env.prod) started 404ing ("model
  unavailable for free") during this scenario's setup on 2026-08-28;
  "minimax/minimax-m3:free" was tried next but also started 404ing/429ing
  within the same day. "minimax/minimax-m2.7:free" is what's actually
  configured and live-tested working as of 2026-08-28, picked after
  live-testing several free chat models directly against
  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions (curl) for one that actually
  returns a clean, non-empty completion instead of erroring or burning its
  token budget on hidden reasoning tokens. OpenRouter's free tier is
  unstable enough that this model may also stop working later -- curl
  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models | jq to list current free models and
  re-test before assuming this value is still correct.

  isDefault: true puts this ahead of any other active chat config in the
  fallback chain (ProviderSelectionService, priority = isDefault DESC,
  updatedAt DESC) -- it does not disable other configs, they just become
  fallbacks.
}
